  "result": "If I could change the world in one way, I\u2019d give every person the ability to truly feel another\u2019s experience\u2014joys, fears, pain and hope alike. Imagine if, whenever someone suffered hunger, loneliness or injustice, you actually felt that ache in your own heart. Or if, when someone celebrated a dream fulfilled, the same rush of warmth lit up your mind.  \n\nThat single change\u2014universal, visceral empathy\u2014would transform everything:  \n\u2022 Conflict would collapse under the weight of shared feeling.  \n\u2022 Poverty, discrimination and indifference would become unthinkable, because you\u2019d feel their impact on yourself.  \n\u2022 Cooperation and generosity would follow naturally, since helping others would inescapably feel like helping yourself.  \n\nIn a world wired this way, every policy, every choice, every innovation would start from the same foundation: \u201cHow does this touch each of us?\u201d And we\u2019d build our societies around connection, care and collective well-being rather than competition or division.  \n",
